{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"roman: Roman numeral conversion.\"\"\"\nVALUES = {\"I\": 1, \"V\": 5, \"X\": 10, \"L\": 50, \"C\": 100, \"D\": 500, \"M\": 1000}\n\n\ndef to_int(text):\n    total = 0\n    prev_value = 0\n    for ch in reversed(text):\n        value = VALUES[ch]\n        if value < prev_value:\n            total -= value\n        else:\n            total += value\n        prev_value = value\n    return total\n","expected_sha256":"1eabf913364356c5c6463802383d7a2aa2cdc25fb29652a22ed4d57dc38d39d4","kind":"modify","path":"src/roman.py"}],"rationale":"Updated to_int to handle subtractive notation by iterating from right to left and subtracting when a smaller value precedes a larger one, correctly converting numerals like IV and MCMXCIV."}